# Pandas CSV Data Analysis

```python
import pandas as pd

# Create student data
data = {
    "name": ["Aravinth", "Vishnu", "Arun", "Jacob", "Titus"],
    "age": [18, 19, 21, 20, 22],
    "marks": [75, 88, 65, 92, 81]
}

# Create DataFrame
df = pd.DataFrame(data)

# Save DataFrame as CSV
df.to_csv("students.csv", index=False)  #this index=false prevents pandas can add extra column to dataframe

# Read CSV file
df = pd.read_csv("students.csv")

# Display students with marks >= 80
print("Students with marks >= 80:")
print(df[df["marks"] >= 80][["name", "marks"]])

# Calculate average marks
print("\nAverage marks:")
print(df["marks"].mean())

# Find the topper
print("\nTopper:")
print(df.loc[df["marks"].idxmax(), ["name", "marks"]])

# Display students with marks >= 75
print("\nStudents with marks >= 75:")
print(df[df["marks"] >= 75][["name", "marks"]])

# Sort students from highest to lowest marks
print("\nStudents sorted by marks:")
print(df.sort_values(by="marks", ascending=False))
```

## Concepts Practiced

* Creating a Pandas DataFrame
* Saving DataFrame to CSV using `to_csv()`
* Reading CSV using `read_csv()`
* Filtering rows
* Selecting columns
* Finding average using `mean()`
* Finding the maximum index using `idxmax()`
* Sorting data using `sort_values()`

## CSV Workflow

```text
